  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.8.0 hardens disclosure when a policy meets a runtime error, for example from a data source's quirks, without giving up query plan optimisation.\n\n      - **Casts and floating-point arithmetic in policies:** CAST(level AS INTEGER) <= 2 works as a row filter, and ROUND(score * 4, 0) / 4 as a mask. A mask or placeholder that can fail is refused when the engine is created, naming the rule and the call.\n      - **Settled closed:** a row filter that fails for a row leaves it out; a rule condition that fails falls through to the next rule. What cannot be settled stops the query with PolicyIndeterminateException, naming the table and a correlation id, never the value.\n      - **Observer:** WithEntitlements(options, audit:, indeterminate:) takes an IIndeterminateDecisions that hears each decision with its reason, a count and the correlation id.\n      - **Databases:** a policy's part that can fail is evaluated by ChalkQL, not sent; a database that fails anyway before returning a row has its table read again and the policy evaluated here. Maintained views settle the same way at each update.\n      - **Fixes:** AND, OR and CASE WHEN evaluate later operands only for undecided rows; casts in comparisons are kept in SQL sent to sources (SQLite had compared text); a pushed row filter under a pruning projection is recognised; a BOOLEAN mask on a path-entitled table prepares for a context's shape.\n      - **Compatibility:** new API for indeterminate decisions. The IR gains Rel.quarantine and GUARDED: a 0.8 engine refuses an entitled plan from an earlier planner, so upgrade ChalkQL and ChalkQL.Sources together. A query a raising policy condition used to fail now answers.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.8.0",
